    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 0,
        "line": 2,
        "text": "We think of America as a completely divided country. Red states and blue states, of course -- but also blue cities within red states, and red neighborhoods in those blue cities. So we’ve assumed it’s our geography that’s dividing us."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 3,
        "line": 1016,
        "text": "One time Paris was six years old and she was singing along to a song on the radio and I said -- you know, with a laugh -- “You really can’t carry a tune, can you?” And she never sang again, not even “Happy Birthday.” It’s all regrets."
      }
    },
